{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Unto all the congregation of… saying…</b> One needs to know to whom the children of Israel are to say it. And perhaps it is because Moses did not speak with the women and the little ones, even though they were there, and He commanded to say the things to them." "And the verse's saying <b>this is the thing</b> etc. <b>saying</b> — it is explained in light of what they said in Sifrei (parashat Ki Tetze): Rabbi Meir says: ״Better that you not vow״ — better than this and than that is not to vow at all. Rabbi Yehudah says: better than this and than that is one who vows and fulfills. End quote. And they said in chapter 1 of Nedarim (Nedarim 9a) two resolutions: the first, that they disagree concerning a vow, but concerning a freewill offering Rabbi Meir concedes that one may volunteer and fulfill, and that is in a case where it does not lead to stumbling, like the practice of Hillel who would bring his offering as unconsecrated animal to the Temple courtyard and there he would consecrate it. And the second, that they disagree even concerning a freewill offering, and Rabbi Yehudah said only one may volunteer but not vow, and even volunteering only specifically in a manner that does not lead to stumbling as mentioned above; see there. According to this, the verse intends to speak along this line: since it preceded by saying ״Take from among you an offering, whoever is of a willing heart״ — if so, the verse is speaking of a freewill offering. Therefore it says <b>this is the thing</b>, meaning: the freewill offering — HaShem commanded <b>to say</b> it, meaning, specifically under this condition, which is what HaShem commanded: that you say it — one volunteers and fulfills, and it is in a manner that does not lead to stumbling. According to the first resolution, our approach follows Rabbi Meir, and according to the second resolution, it follows Rabbi Yehudah."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:47.902603184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}